      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The sub-Weyl critical-line estimate is logarithmically encoded as J(t) and inserted into a detector specialized to the fixed lines sigma=1/2 and sigma=3/2; positivity, coefficient-sign cancellation, and Laplace-transform monotonicity close the detector inequality, which an extremal barrier argument turns into the stated intermediate O(1/log t) zero-free region.",
