      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A normalized squared-modulus parameterization makes global non-negativity of the trigonometric polynomial automatic, while autocorrelation exposes the proof-facing coefficients; heuristic annealing can therefore search the remaining finite admissibility constraints and theorem objectives, with published rounded coefficients preserving an inspectable candidate record.",
